==Battleground==
*1 [[Wicked Tank Cat (Enemy)|Wicked Tank Cat]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*6 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*4 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 93.33~96.67 seconds<sup>2,800f~2,900f</sup>.
*2 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 93.33~96.67 seconds<sup>2,800f~2,900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Try to stall Wicked Tank Cat so that it gains as little ground as possible, whether with meatshields or something like [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper Cat]]. Due to Wicked Tank's Surge Attacks, it is strongly recommended to use [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge Immune units]]: however, non-Uber options at this point in progression are few and far between.

If you made it this far to actually unlock this stage, then you should be easily able to beat most of the supporting enemies; however, the Aku Gories will provide some difficulty, due to their tankiness and overall high damage. Use strong mid-rangers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] to get rid of them as soon as possible.

